00:41:00,681 --> 00:41:05,420
because that's a very biologically rich area for plants and wildlife.

523
00:41:06,620 --> 00:41:12,480
Overall, we planted about 3,000 seedlings here on the floodplains,

524
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:14,800
all wetland species from the area.

525
00:41:16,540 --> 00:41:21,500
People that drive by this site would never know there was a dam here.

526
00:41:21,501 --> 00:41:25,060
It is tremendously gratifying and exciting for me

527
00:41:25,061 --> 00:41:29,160
to be able to see the Merced River in its free-flowing state

528
00:41:29,161 --> 00:41:31,940
and to be a truly wild and scenic river.

529
00:41:34,080 --> 00:41:38,400
Finally, after so many decades, the river flows freely.

530
00:41:39,820 --> 00:41:42,260
This natural state is healthier for rivers,

531
00:41:42,980 --> 00:41:46,820
but the passing water is an increasingly valuable resource for humankind.

532
00:41:47,720 --> 00:41:53,300
And as a result, dams will continue to hold their place in the midst of our waterways.

